Thanks for flagging @w0xlt, my own LLM scans also came up with the same two issues yesterday :). I think both revolve around the question whether we can provide a function that is robust against adversary-provided, or otherwise incorrectly constructed coins. My current impression is that we cannot. For your second suggestion, how about just amending the documentation with "coins must be unspent and their height below the blocks height"?

The first one is a bit annoying to deal with. We could just assume that "these coins are required to be genuine", but the caches are just annoying in general and don't really serve a purpose in the context of validating a single block. Maybe we can clear them every time we call the function? I really don't want to add more code to the existing validation functions.
